"""DEEP16 pipeline 2 (generated art): the art desk's basilisk pages -> basilisk_p1, a creature new to the grid (10-22, the monster cutter seat's
third run, on Griz's "close the desk but have the cutter run us out of usage for the week. See y'all tueday").

    python tools/basilisk-sheet.py            # deep16/art/basilisk_p1.png + .json

Sources (the art desk's, in the main checkout's deep16/_src/basilisk/ART-17/ -- a worktree reads them there): ART-17 (10-21), all five views
in one delivery, one action a page on two printed bands (Flinch and Prone on one): HEAD 1 SE (its page 1 an identity sheet, not cut), HEAD 2
NE, HEAD 3 S, HEAD 4 E, HEAD 5 N; Idle 6, Walk 8, Gaze 6, Bite 6, Flinch 4, Fall 6, Prone 2. The pages' names carry their view and action
(ART-17_HEAD-1_PAGE-2_SE_Idle.png): _src/art-desk/sort-delivery.py did not take them for pages, so the seat copied them out of the received
folder, each sha256 checked against the zip's manifest.
What each became: idle, walk, gaze (js/traits.js M.gazeSave plays it as the gaze falls), attack <- Bite, flinch, hurt <- Fall (played once),
prone <- Prone played backwards. Facings: the five views as drawn, SW, W and NW the mirrors of SE, E and NE.
The boxes by the seat's draft (each page's bodies clustered into the manifest's printed bands; each frame's x its body's middle -- the
numbers sit beside the long tails and claws, too faint for the reader; each strip from 30 px over the highest foot to the next band, so the
digits and labels beside the feet blank whole; the white letters and soft digits boxed besides).
Cut, scaled and placed by tools/artdesk.py. Its size (the seat's call): 32 px side-on (a long, low eight-legged lizard, its head up), 40 from
the front and from behind -- the identity page's stills disagree with themselves (front 341, side 235, back 446 px; the art desk calls them
inadequate), so not by them. A later page by its first frame against its view's Idle 1, a Fall page by its Fall 1, a Prone page by its
Prone 2 if it stands (else its Prone 1 -- see STAND_OF). Two passes: the second tones every page per channel to its own view's first-pass
idle, the SE and NE to the E's.
"""
import os, sys, json
import importlib.util
import numpy as np
from PIL import Image

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
def _load(name):
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, os.path.join(ROOT, 'tools', name + '.py'))
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod
pix, AD = _load('pixelate'), _load('artdesk')

NAME = 'basilisk_p1'
FW, FH, AX, AY = 112, 54, 56, 50            # (E's bite and tail 54 px each side, S's crest 48 up)
STAND = {'side': 32, 'S': 40, 'N': 40}

def R(*rows):
    """a page's rows: (row, band, label strip, n, xs) -> artdesk's rows and the numbers by hand"""
    return [(r, b, s, n) for r, b, s, n, _ in rows], {r: xs for r, _, _, _, xs in rows}

